><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250630092042+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250630092045+10'00'" name="2aad39b9-6ad8-4ab2-921e-e9e74939b2ec" page="5" coords="62.589005,172.697403,294.657074,172.697403,62.589005,162.341492,294.657074,162.341492,62.589005,161.699326,294.676910,161.699326,62.589005,151.343414,294.676910,151.343414,62.589005,150.757767,294.639160,150.757767,62.589005,140.401855,294.639160,140.401855,62.589005,139.816177,294.674591,139.816177,62.589005,129.460266,294.674591,129.460266,62.589005,128.818115,294.693573,128.818115,62.589005,118.462204,294.693573,118.462204,62.589005,117.876541,294.653320,117.876541,62.589005,107.520630,294.653320,107.520630,62.589005,106.934967,294.659149,106.934967,62.589005,96.579056,294.659149,96.579056,62.589005,95.936905,294.691162,95.936905,62.589005,85.580994,294.691162,85.580994,62.589005,84.995331,294.681030,84.995331,62.589005,74.639420,294.681030,74.639420,62.589005,74.053757,294.673126,74.053757,62.589005,63.697845,294.673126,63.697845,62.589005,63.055695,200.800415,63.055695,62.589005,52.699783,200.800415,52.699783" rect="62.265381,52.376160,295.017212,173.021027" subject="Comment on Text" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Our results suggest that a single bout of IPC has meaningful&#xD;benefits on 1,000-m kayak performance for well-trained male&#xD;kayak athletes. However, in a competition context consisting&#xD;of multiple events, it seems that the effect of the initial IPC&#xD;application may washout after an initial maximal effort. Although&#xD;a secondary repeated IPC treatment can provide a topup&#xD;effect, scheduling multiple 40 minutes IPC interventions&#xD;20–40 minutes before races with limited preparation time may&#xD;not be practical in a real world scenario. Therefore, practitioners&#xD;may look to save IPC treatments for higher priority&#xD;races (semi-finals, finals) in practice.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="5" rect="612.000000,80.697403,796.000000,172.697403"
/></highlight
